# Background
This is a descriptive summary of contact degree of the India GlobalMix diary data.

# Method
We adapted the code Maria developed for the CorporateMix data to the GlobalMix data to calculate degree information. The degree information is summarized by urban-rural and home-nonhome statuses, which are the two putative predictors of mixing. We excluded contacts lasted ≤ 15 mins in analysis. The degree information was summarized as the average degree of the two-day visits. Given the data were egocentric, we use $M.D.=\frac{edges}{n}$ for the relationship between mean degree ($M.D.$) and the number of edges.


```{r, echo=F, warning=F, message=FALSE}
