## Characterization of home-nonhome status
The home-nonhome status is processed from multiple questions asking contact location; given these questions are not mutually exclusive, a contact is characterized as at home when any contact with a participant reportedly occurred at the contact's home or other's home, regardless of the responses for other contact locations. For contacts did not occurred at home, they were characterized as occurring in a nonhome location if any of the nonhome locations were checked. For a contact checked neither home nor nonhome location, we assigned an NA to this contact. Below is a breakdown of the frequency of contact, in which there was `r paste0(as.numeric(round(tb_contact_location[3]/nrow(india_mix)*100)), "%")` of contact did not check any of the contact locations. We excluded these contacts in analysis.
