## Total degree by participants' age group
The below figure shows the total degree of contact in each participant's age group by putative predictor of mixing. The total degree peaked in the age group of 10-14 years old and gradually became lower in the adjacent age groups. For participants < 1 year old, the total degree of 6-11 months old was slightly lower than those < 6 months old.

The participant's total degree tended to be higher at home than non-home locations, except the degrees were similar between the two age groups between 10-19 years old. 

The total degrees were similar between those reside in urban and non-urban areas for the three age groups between 5-19 years old. For the other age groups, the total degree tended to be higher in urban than in non-urban settings.


