## Symmetrical mixing matrices
Descriptively, the mixing degree at home were generally higher and more heterogeneous than nonhome settings. For mixings within the same age group, the age group of 10-14y had the highest degree; this age group also had the highest degree among all age group combinations in nonhome settings and urban/rural settings. Compared to the variation between home and nonhome settings, the mixing in urban settings is relatively similar to the mixing in rural settings. Generally, the mixings of adult age groups (≥20y) with their counterparts of any age tended to have higher degrees than the younger age groups (≤19y).

